AL DETAILS...\n- Periods of heavy rainfall, associated with remnant moisture from\nHurricane Polo, are expected to produce numerous showers and\nembedded thunderstorms. Heavy rain falling on saturated soils and\nburn scars could lead to localized flash flooding and rises on\nlocal rivers.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-30T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ed9ede493b5b1546377a5ccc5f8c64d7cb67cd19.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ed9ede493b5b1546377a5ccc5f8c64d7cb67cd19.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-28T19:57:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 281957 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 157 PM MDT Mon Sep 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered to widespread precipitation showers and storms are expected through midweek. - This rainfall increases flooding concerns, especially within and adjacent to the southern San Juans. - A Flood Watch is in effect for southeast Utah and southwest Colo","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-28T19:09:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Deep moisture will continue to stream in from the southwest bringing widespread rain and a few embedded thunderstorms over the next few days. A Flood Watch has been issued for southeast UT and southwest CO due to the increased rainfall and flooding risks. All the clouds and precipitation will keep fire weather concerns to a minimum. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHO","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&f